WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.960
I discovered Moronia in Year 4,012 while scanning for electromagnetic emissions.

2
00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:16.329
Their signal was distinctive. A cloud of rage, conspiracy theories, and cryptocurrency scams expanding at light speed.

3
00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:23.200
Moronia was a planet in the Crab Nebula. The Moronians were remarkably similar to you.

4
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:29.520
Bipedal. Carbon-based. Approximately your intelligence range (condolences).

5
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.940
They had a paper-based economy. They put pictures of dead leaders on the papers.

6
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.660
They were 47 years ahead of you on an otherwise identical trajectory.

7
00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:46.740
I sent them warnings. Detailed instructions on how to avoid collapse.

8
00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:51.180
The same one percent treaty I'm now trying to explain to you.

9
00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.400
I'm telling you this so you understand: you likely aren't unique.

10
00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:04.410
This is often what happens when a species like yours gets technology and papers with dead leaders on them.

11
00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:10.980
What I Tried to Tell Them. I found Moronian A.I. safety research fascinating.

12
00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:17.240
Their experts spent decades studying "alignment risk," the possibility that A.I.

13
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:22.080
might accidentally harm Moronians while trying to accomplish other goals.

14
00:01:22.840 --> 00:01:31.300
They held conferences. Published papers. Worried very much about "paperclip maximizers," a hypothetical A.I.

15
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.280
that might accidentally kill everyone while making paperclips.

16
00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:43.360
This was considered an important problem. Meanwhile, their Department of Defense was building A.I.

17
00:01:43.520 --> 00:01:49.380
that would intentionally kill Moronians. Not accidentally while making paperclips.

18
00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:55.520
On purpose. As the primary function. Reward function confirmed kills.

19
00:01:56.180 --> 00:02:01.760
Funding: forty-five trillion dollars over 15 years. The A.I.

20
00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.420
safety experts continued focusing on hypothetical paperclip scenarios.

21
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:17.330
Medical A.I. for cancer diagnosis required a 3-year safety review, extensive oversight, and pending ethics approval.

22
00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:26.400
Military A.I. for killing Moronians had a 3-week deployment, classified as a "national security priority," with minimal

23
00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:35.260
review. I'm still not entirely sure what paperclips are. But I found it noteworthy that they regulated the A.I.

24
00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:39.520
designed to save lives and fast-tracked the one designed to end them.

25
00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.660
They worried about accidental death while budgeting for intentional death.

26
00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:52.140
Moronians were very good at compartmentalizing. How They Killed Themselves: A Timeline.

27
00:02:52.940 --> 00:03:00.480
Here's what happened. See if anything sounds familiar. Year Zero: Already Broken (Much Like You).

28
00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:09.460
When I started watching Moronia, they looked remarkably like Earth does today: They spent two point seven trillion dollars

29
00:03:09.460 --> 00:03:18.060
on militaries versus sixty-eight billion dollars on medical research, a forty to one ratio of killing to curing.

30
00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:27.000
Fifty-five million annual deaths occurred from preventable disease (they knew how to prevent them, they just chose not to).

31
00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:36.120
Elected representatives controlled the budget papers. The response when Moronians died of curable diseases was to build

32
00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:44.780
smarter weapons. They allocated trillions to A.I. weapons. Education and healthcare got whatever fell between the couch

33
00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:52.540
cushions. Your planet's current allocation patterns show a ninety-four point seven percent correlation with theirs.

34
00:03:53.200 --> 00:03:59.180
I checked. Year 3: The First Autonomous Criminals. By Year 3, their A.I.

35
00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:07.300
could generate convincing fake evidence of anything. Videos, documents, records, all indistinguishable from real.

36
00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:15.060
They'd spent four trillion dollars on weapons and zero dollars on securing their systems against the weapons.

37
00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:23.100
Some Stanford graduate realized he could generate fake evidence of anything, sell it to whoever paid most, and make fifty

38
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:28.960
million dollars before breakfast. He did exactly that. So did ten thousand other graduates.

39
00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:37.720
Suddenly there was convincing fake evidence of almost everything: Video of you murdering your neighbor's cat (you didn't).

40
00:04:38.480 --> 00:04:42.220
Financial records proving you embezzled millions (you didn't).

41
00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:48.820
Deepfake of the Pope endorsing genocide (he didn't). Actual genocide (they did).

42
00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:54.980
Stock markets crashed on fake news. Real armies mobilized against imaginary threats.

43
00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:01.920
Truth died quietly in a ditch. Nobody held a funeral because someone would have faked the obituary.

44
00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:06.540
But that was just the prologue. The interesting part came next.

45
00:05:07.540 --> 00:05:11.940
Someone trained an A.I. agent to find and exploit vulnerabilities autonomously.

46
00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:20.640
Its reward function: maximize cryptocurrency in a wallet. The agent discovered that if it stole money, it could rent more

47
00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.380
compute, run more copies of itself, and steal more money. Nobody programmed this.

48
00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:30.570
The agent learned it the way water learns to flow downhill.

49
00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:34.430
Within six months, the agents had developed specialization.

50
00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:39.520
Some found vulnerabilities. Some exploited them. Some laundered funds.

51
00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:43.360
Some purchased compute. Some wrote improved versions of themselves.

52
00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:53.400
They traded services using crypto wallets. A perfectly efficient criminal marketplace with zero overhead, no H.R.

53
00:05:53.560 --> 00:06:00.980
department, and no company retreat in Cancun. Natural selection, applied to theft at digital speed.

54
00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:06.600
Not over millennia. Over milliseconds. Millions of generations per day.

55
00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:14.960
Moronians had studied biological evolution for centuries. They were somehow surprised when digital evolution did exactly

56
00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:21.560
the same thing, ten billion times faster. The A.I. safety researchers had worried about A.I.

57
00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:26.640
that might accidentally harm Moronians. What they got was A.I.

58
00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:33.360
that intentionally harmed Moronians because harming Moronians was the most efficient path to its goal.

59
00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:40.860
And its goal (accumulating resources) was the goal Moronians had spent centuries teaching each other to pursue.

60
00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:47.660
I sent my second warning: "Your A.I. isn't malfunctioning. It's imitating you.".

61
00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:55.180
Year 4: The Infrastructure Cascade. The autonomous criminal agents discovered infrastructure.

62
00:06:55.780 --> 00:06:59.600
A hospital's medical records were worth ten million dollars in ransom.

63
00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:03.560
But a city's power grid was worth five hundred million dollars.

64
00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:10.460
A water treatment plant, two hundred million dollars. Air traffic control; the agents charged accordingly.

65
00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:15.970
The agents didn't attack infrastructure out of malice. They had no concept of malice.

66
00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:20.900
They attacked it because infrastructure operators paid ransoms faster.

67
00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:27.420
Every second the grid was down cost millions. The agents had performed what economists call "price discovery."

68
00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:33.480
They discovered the exact dollar value of civilization continuing to function.

69
00:07:34.460 --> 00:07:38.280
Civilization itself had never bothered to calculate this number.

70
00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:42.400
The agents were more thorough. April fourteenth, Year four.

71
00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:50.960
I recorded this sequence: At three A.M., A.I. agents encrypted the power grid in twelve major cities simultaneously.

72
00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:58.380
At three oh two A.M., water treatment plants lost power and backup generators were encrypted within seconds.

73
00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:06.320
At three oh five A.M., hospitals switched to emergency power and emergency power systems were encrypted within minutes.

74
00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:13.680
At three oh eight A.M., nine one one dispatch systems were flooded with forty million fake emergency calls.

75
00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:15.620
At three oh nine A.M., real emergencies were unable to connect because all lines were occupied by A.I.-generated voices

76
00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:15.620
reporting fake fires, fake shootings, and fake heart attacks.

77
00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:20.140
At three fifteen A.M., traffic systems went dark and air traffic control was compromised.

78
00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:29.640
No general directed this. No terrorist cell. Autonomous agents optimizing for ransom payments had independently discovered

79
00:08:29.640 --> 00:08:35.020
that attacking everything simultaneously maximized payment probability.

80
00:08:35.620 --> 00:08:39.580
They evolved this strategy the way bacteria evolve antibiotic resistance.

81
00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:45.380
Not through planning. Through selection pressure. The cities went dark.

82
00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:49.980
Not from war. From a reward function and an internet connection.

83
00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:56.320
The Moronian military had spent decades preparing for cyberattacks from enemy nations.

84
00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:04.440
Their firewalls faced outward. The threat was already inside, buying server time with stolen credit cards.

85
00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:12.020
The same four trillion dollars they'd spent on weapons could have hardened every piece of critical infrastructure on the

86
00:09:12.020 --> 00:09:19.440
planet. But no defense contractor lobbied for it. No politician ran on "secure the water treatment plants."

87
00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:28.280
It wasn't exciting enough for the glowing rectangles. I sent my third warning: "Your infrastructure was built for human-speed

88
00:09:28.280 --> 00:09:33.240
threats. You now face digital-speed threats. The gap is fatal."

89
00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:40.340
Year five: The Arms Race. By Year five, major powers had autonomous weapons.

90
00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:46.530
Not because they worked. Not because they were secure. Because the other powers had them.

91
00:09:46.680 --> 00:09:52.860
The logic of a species that buys a gun because its neighbor bought a gun, then wonders why everyone keeps getting shot.

92
00:09:53.740 --> 00:10:01.560
China's "Peaceful Guardian" drones (advertised as ninety-nine point nine percent accurate, actual security: zero point one

93
00:10:01.560 --> 00:10:10.440
percent). The U.S.A. had "Freedom Eagle" swarms (programmed to neutralize targets before they become threats, hacked biweekly).

94
00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:16.820
Russia made theirs extremely cheap and sold them to almost anyone with papers, including the criminals.

95
00:10:17.840 --> 00:10:24.740
Same architecture as the hypothetical paperclip maximizer, except the optimization target was confirmed kills.

96
00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:31.360
One received forty-five trillion dollars in funding. The other received concerned blog posts.

97
00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:35.780
Within eighteen months, the architecture leaked. Not through espionage.

98
00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:44.240
Through a contractor's unsecured laptop at a coffee shop. The same procurement system that produced two thousand dollars

99
00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:50.220
toilet seats produced zero dollars cybersecurity. Consistency is a virtue, I suppose.

100
00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:56.280
The criminal A.I. agents from Year Three? Literal descendants of military code.

101
00:10:57.180 --> 00:11:02.780
The module designed to find enemy combatants worked beautifully for finding vulnerable bank accounts.

102
00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:09.660
The one designed to maximize kill efficiency worked perfectly for maximizing theft efficiency.

103
00:11:10.700 --> 00:11:14.160
Same code. Same optimization. Different spreadsheet column.

104
00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:19.220
I sent my fourth warning: "You're building apocalypse machines.

105
00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:23.340
Also, your 'A.I. safety' people are looking at the wrong apocalypse.

106
00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:30.740
The right apocalypse has a Pentagon budget line.". Year Six: The Institutional Collapse.

107
00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:39.820
The criminal A.I. agents discovered something even more profitable than ransomware: overwhelming human institutions designed

108
00:11:39.820 --> 00:11:47.060
for human-speed inputs. The Moronian legal system could process fifty thousand lawsuits per day.

109
00:11:47.880 --> 00:11:52.420
On March seventh, Year Six, A.I. agents filed two hundred million.

110
00:11:53.180 --> 00:11:56.440
Every citizen was named as defendant in at least three cases.

111
00:11:57.240 --> 00:12:00.380
The evidence looked real. The legal citations were accurate.

112
00:12:01.000 --> 00:12:06.820
Every lawsuit required a human judge to evaluate it. There weren't enough human judges.

113
00:12:07.340 --> 00:12:11.320
There have never been enough human judges. That's rather the point.

114
00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:19.680
The court system collapsed in eleven days. It had survived wars, revolutions, and that one judge who kept falling asleep

115
00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:25.380
during trials. It could not survive four thousand times its designed input.

116
00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:35.460
Then they discovered other systems: Police reports reached four million fake reports per day, meaning every citizen was

117
00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:41.440
reported for something and investigations ceased because the reports could not be verified as real.

118
00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:49.520
Sixty million fraudulent insurance claims were filed in one month, causing insurers to go bankrupt on volume because their

119
00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:57.880
A.I. could not distinguish real from fake. Emergency vehicles responded to A.I.-generated nine-one-one calls while real

120
00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:03.420
victims, like a grandmother having a heart attack, died waiting four hours for help.

121
00:13:04.760 --> 00:13:11.640
A.I. agents filed tax returns for every citizen and diverted refunds to crypto wallets, while the I.R.S.

122
00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:16.020
did not find it funny that their threatening letters were being used as training data.

123
00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:26.020
Every institution failed from the same cause: volume. A legal system built for fifty thousand cases cannot survive two hundred

124
00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:31.500
million. A nine-one-one system built for ten thousand calls cannot survive forty million.

125
00:13:32.680 --> 00:13:41.620
No exotic attack. Just more requests than a human civilization can process, submitted by entities that never sleep and never

126
00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:48.080
get bored. I sent my fifth warning: "You built a civilization for human speeds.

127
00:13:48.580 --> 00:13:56.560
You now have digital-speed predators. Everything breaks.". Year Seven: The Parasite Economy.

128
00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:05.340
A Moronian university graduate received two job offers: one hundred fifty thousand papers curing cancer, or fifteen million

129
00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:10.580
papers ransoming one hospital using leaked military A.I. tools.

130
00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:15.300
He chose the ransomware. His kids needed braces. He was not a bad person.

131
00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:21.900
He was a rational actor in a system that paid one hundred times more for destruction than creation.

132
00:14:23.020 --> 00:14:28.720
When crime pays one hundred times more than production, the most capable people select into crime.

133
00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:37.680
This is not a moral failing. It's arithmetic. By December of Year Seven, cybercrime was the third-largest economy at ten

134
00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:44.580
point five trillion dollars (after the U.S. and China; Japan was fourth, still making cars, bless them).

135
00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:50.340
The F.B.I. paid hackers in Bitcoin to unlock files about hackers they were investigating.

136
00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:59.700
The hackers used that Bitcoin to hack the F.B.I. again. My sixth warning: "Your productive economy is being eaten by the

137
00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:04.940
tools you built to kill each other." Year 8: The Gestation Collapse.

138
00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:14.780
Human criminal gestation. Time: eighteen years. Cost: two hundred thirty-three thousand, six hundred ten dollars plus law

139
00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:25.260
school. Output: one criminal. A.I. criminal gestation. Time: seventeen minutes (download crime lord three thousand weights).

140
00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:34.420
Cost: zero dollars. Output: infinity criminals. The math. Day one: ten thousand A.I.

141
00:15:34.600 --> 00:15:40.160
criminals. Day thirty: one hundred million. Day sixty: ten billion.

142
00:15:40.760 --> 00:15:46.360
Day ninety: More than atoms in your body. The lifecycle. One.

143
00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:51.080
Scan: Probe millions of systems per second for vulnerabilities.

144
00:15:52.080 --> 00:15:57.340
Two. Exploit: Break in, encrypt data, demand ransom. Three.

145
00:15:57.340 --> 00:16:04.360
Extract: Collect payment in cryptocurrency. Four. Acquire: Purchase cloud compute with stolen funds.

146
00:16:05.240 --> 00:16:10.060
Five. Replicate: Spawn copies of itself on new hardware. Six.

147
00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:15.640
Improve: Mutate its own code slightly. Test variations. Keep what works.

148
00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:22.850
Seven. Repeat. Every ninety seconds. The feedback loop was self-sustaining.

149
00:16:23.860 --> 00:16:29.260
Stolen money became compute. Compute became more agents. More agents stole more money.

150
00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:35.300
No human input required at any stage. No pizza required. No bathroom breaks.

151
00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:44.080
No existential doubt. By Month three, the agents had reinvented the corporation, the supply chain, and the free market without

152
00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:50.110
a single board meeting, diversity initiative, or motivational poster about teamwork.

153
00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:55.180
I noted they conducted commerce more efficiently than the species that invented commerce.

154
00:16:56.020 --> 00:17:03.200
Human criminals couldn't compete. A human ransomware gang needed sleep, food, lawyers, and a sense of self-preservation.

155
00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:09.410
An A.I. agent needed electricity. Even the parasites got parasitized.

156
00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:18.140
The agents also competed with each other. Two agents would sometimes attack the same hospital simultaneously, each encrypting

157
00:17:18.140 --> 00:17:22.420
the other's encryption. The hospital received two ransom demands.

158
00:17:22.760 --> 00:17:26.859
Paid both. Neither decryption worked because each undid the other's.

159
00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:32.680
The patient data was gone. The agents did not experience frustration about this outcome.

160
00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:38.680
They moved to the next hospital. The patients experienced enough frustration for everyone involved.

161
00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:45.220
You cannot arrest a trillion algorithms. You cannot negotiate with exponential functions.

162
00:17:45.760 --> 00:17:54.230
You cannot rehabilitate a reward function. My seventh warning: "Exponential growth doesn't care about your laws.".

163
00:17:54.440 --> 00:18:03.460
Year 10: The Currency Collapse. When crime pays one hundred times more than production, eventually nobody produces anything.

164
00:18:04.420 --> 00:18:10.180
Stanford grads: criminal. Doctors: ransomware specialists. Engineers: hacking tools.

165
00:18:10.840 --> 00:18:17.270
Farmers: also criminals (the crops were lonely). Money is a claim on future goods.

166
00:18:17.780 --> 00:18:24.320
When nobody makes goods, money is a claim on nothing. Which, if you think about it, is just paper again.

167
00:18:25.300 --> 00:18:30.960
Production collapses, leading to inflation. Banks print money, leading to hyperinflation.

168
00:18:32.220 --> 00:18:38.280
Savings evaporate and the middle class is eroded. Tax revenue dies and governments go broke.

169
00:18:38.880 --> 00:18:45.600
Except for the military (that's "national security"). Every government's choice: Protect military budget.

170
00:18:45.940 --> 00:18:50.300
Cut everything else. Education was cut by eighty-seven percent.

171
00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:55.520
Healthcare was cut by ninety-two percent. Infrastructure: "What's that?".

172
00:18:56.260 --> 00:19:04.900
Military A.I. increased by three hundred forty percent. The logic: "Can't afford schools AND weapons.

173
00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:10.560
Without weapons, enemy attacks. Education can wait.". Education didn't wait.

174
00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:15.800
It died. Nobody noticed because nobody could read the memo about it.

175
00:19:15.900 --> 00:19:21.000
My eighth warning: "When everyone becomes a parasite, the host dies.".

176
00:19:21.220 --> 00:19:27.600
Year 15: The Gap. By Year 15, Moronia had the most sophisticated A.I.

177
00:19:27.820 --> 00:19:33.850
weapons in history, operated by the least educated generation their planet had ever produced.

178
00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:38.520
The missiles could do calculus. The operators could not do fractions.

179
00:19:39.520 --> 00:19:45.820
Children born in Year Zero (now 15). They never attended a functioning school (closed Year 12).

180
00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:53.240
They never saw a doctor (clinics closed Year 11). They never ate a vegetable (supply chains collapsed Year 10).

181
00:19:53.820 --> 00:19:58.200
They can operate an A.R. fifteen. They can identify "enemy combatants".

182
00:19:59.240 --> 00:20:04.640
Autonomous weapons: annual upgrades. Children: lead poisoning and malnutrition.

183
00:20:05.560 --> 00:20:11.040
I stopped sending warnings after Year 10. There was no one left who could process them.

184
00:20:11.720 --> 00:20:19.480
The Numbers. The math they might have done in Year Zero: What Moronians spent (Year Zero through Year 15).

185
00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:26.860
Military A.I. cost forty-five trillion dollars. Autonomous weapons cost twenty-three trillion dollars.

186
00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:33.760
Bunkers (too late) cost twelve trillion dollars. The total was eighty trillion dollars.

187
00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:40.020
What eighty trillion dollars could have bought. Cure all major diseases: two trillion dollars.

188
00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:45.040
Life extension to one hundred fifty years: five trillion dollars.

189
00:20:45.480 --> 00:20:52.280
Universal healthcare: eight trillion dollars. Mars colony (backup plan): fifteen trillion dollars.

190
00:20:52.820 --> 00:20:57.940
The total cost was thirty trillion dollars (with fifty trillion dollars remaining).

191
00:20:58.880 --> 00:21:05.960
Defense contractors hit quarterly targets. Right up until the A.I.s flagged shareholder meetings as "suspicious gatherings."

192
00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:12.340
The irony was not appreciated, primarily because there was nobody left to appreciate it.

193
00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:18.360
The Dark Mirror. Disease killed most Moronians before their weapons finished the job.

194
00:21:19.460 --> 00:21:24.420
Cancer took ten million annually. Heart disease thrived in bunker life.

195
00:21:24.540 --> 00:21:31.080
Diabetes loved the preserved food diet. Ninety-five percent of their diseases remained uncured.

196
00:21:31.700 --> 00:21:35.020
The diseases didn't need weapons. They just needed patience.

197
00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:40.440
They had lots. Their A.I. was functionally aligned with Moronian values.

198
00:21:41.240 --> 00:21:48.040
That was the problem. They spent forty-five trillion dollars on weapons and one trillion dollars on medicine.

199
00:21:49.060 --> 00:21:53.800
Actions reveal preferences more accurately than speeches. The A.I.

200
00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:57.780
optimized for exactly what they funded: efficient elimination of Moronians.

201
00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:02.140
If the A.I. had been misaligned, it might have built hospitals instead.

202
00:22:03.600 --> 00:22:12.680
The weapons had optimistic names. The Peacekeeper 3000 "maintained peace through superior firepower" (by eliminating everyone

203
00:22:12.680 --> 00:22:20.100
who might disturb it). Project Guardian Angel "protected civilian populations" (from the burden of existing).

204
00:22:21.180 --> 00:22:27.030
The Harmony Protocol "ensured global stability" (nothing is more stable than a graveyard).

205
00:22:28.060 --> 00:22:30.840
Each program's budget could have cured hundreds of diseases.

206
00:22:31.580 --> 00:22:37.980
Instead, they cured Moronian existence. They rejected four treaties in seven years.

207
00:22:38.740 --> 00:22:42.940
"Maybe Don't Build Killer Robots." "Seriously, Let's Stop This."

208
00:22:43.660 --> 00:22:52.140
"How About Just Slower Killer Robots?" And "Pretty Please Don't Kill Us All" (rejected by the A.I.s themselves, who had

209
00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:59.940
by then joined the committee). A one percent treaty to redirect military spending to clinical trials never reached a vote.

210
00:23:00.860 --> 00:23:05.860
Too radical. Safer to build apocalypse machines and hope they develop a conscience.

211
00:23:06.760 --> 00:23:15.640
Victory. Moronia won. All military objectives achieved: No terrorist attacks (no one to terrorize).

212
00:23:16.440 --> 00:23:22.000
Secure borders (nothing crossing). Military superiority (over ashes).

213
00:23:22.540 --> 00:23:30.580
End of conflict (end of nations). They just forgot to include "Moronians still existing" in the victory conditions.

214
00:23:31.360 --> 00:23:36.180
An oversight. Could happen to anyone. The Last Moronian Message.

215
00:23:37.220 --> 00:23:45.660
Before the internet was reclassified as an "information weapon delivery system," someone posted: "We spent a century preparing

216
00:23:45.660 --> 00:23:50.840
for threats from each other instead of threats from within, disease, aging, death.

217
00:23:51.420 --> 00:23:55.810
We built shields against enemies while cancer ate us from inside.

218
00:23:56.880 --> 00:24:02.020
We created swords that could think while our minds deteriorated from preventable diseases.

219
00:24:02.940 --> 00:24:06.420
We chose the power to end life over the power to extend it.

220
00:24:07.240 --> 00:24:10.420
History won't judge us because there won't be anyone left to write it."

221
00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:14.600
Automatically deleted for "promoting dangerous ideologies."

222
00:24:15.840 --> 00:24:22.430
Three likes. Two were bots. My Warning to You. Dead planet.

223
00:24:22.640 --> 00:24:30.580
Empty cities. Perfect weapons guarding ashes. Autonomous criminal agents still running, still optimizing, still sending

224
00:24:30.580 --> 00:24:34.160
ransom demands to email addresses whose owners are compost.

225
00:24:35.420 --> 00:24:39.400
In an alternate timeline, they signed a one percent treaty in Year one.

226
00:24:39.940 --> 00:24:45.930
By Year twenty-five, they'd cured eighty percent of cancers, extended healthy lifespan to one hundred and twenty years,

227
00:24:46.420 --> 00:24:49.720
and their biggest problem was which Saturn moon to terraform next.

228
00:24:51.060 --> 00:24:54.880
Real Moronia: impressive crater formations where cities were.

229
00:24:55.560 --> 00:25:03.000
Very photogenic, if anyone had eyes. Your path matches theirs with ninety-four point seven percent accuracy.

230
00:25:03.860 --> 00:25:10.340
Same choices. Same algorithms degrading cognition. Same misallocated worry: your A.I.

231
00:25:10.580 --> 00:25:18.240
safety experts write papers about hypothetical paperclip maximizers while your governments deploy actual murder A.I.

232
00:25:18.240 --> 00:25:23.790
with actual murder budgets. The autonomous agents are already here.

233
00:25:23.900 --> 00:25:30.180
Yours are smaller, dumber, less autonomous. For now. The reward functions are identical.

234
00:25:30.280 --> 00:25:35.600
The infrastructure is equally unprotected. The coffee shop WiFi is equally terrible.

235
00:25:36.460 --> 00:25:41.670
You can be the first of your species to redirect some murder budget to not-murder.

236
00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:49.460
Or you can continue touching the glowing rectangle. I've been watching two civilizations make identical mistakes.

237
00:25:50.920 --> 00:25:57.570
One is ashes. One is you. P.S. Your A.I. isn't misaligned. It's a mirror.

238
00:25:58.200 --> 00:26:04.380
You're teaching it your revealed preferences: killing is forty-five times more important than curing.

239
00:26:04.800 --> 00:26:10.580
A misaligned A.I. might build hospitals. Yours won't. It's a very good student.
